1
00:01:04,896 --> 00:01:07,021
Netflix has 200 million subscribers.

2
00:01:07,521 --> 00:01:09,813
Prime Video has 150 million.

3
00:01:10,188 --> 00:01:14,146
Put these two platforms together
and it comes to 350 million viewers,

4
00:01:14,563 --> 00:01:17,021
plus family members,
and multiple users...

5
00:01:17,271 --> 00:01:18,521
That's a lot of people.

6
00:01:19,021 --> 00:01:23,396
It means that by now, in 2020,
these streaming services

7
00:01:23,521 --> 00:01:28,271
define our collective imagination,
the zeitgeist, the spirit of our times...

8
00:01:29,271 --> 00:01:33,021
But then there's Pornhub,
the porn content streamer

9
00:01:33,146 --> 00:01:36,021
with 42 billion visitors per year.

10
00:01:36,146 --> 00:01:39,563
3.5 billion a month,
115 million every day.

11
00:01:40,896 --> 00:01:44,646
Netflix, Prime Video and other platforms
represent our public discourse.

12
00:01:45,313 --> 00:01:48,271
But Pornhub is the unconscious,
it's what we repress,

13
00:01:49,271 --> 00:01:51,021
it's what society doesn't show,

14
00:01:52,021 --> 00:01:53,813
what we really are.

15
00:01:57,063 --> 00:01:59,396
That's how this whole story started.

16
00:01:59,813 --> 00:02:01,688
The way you start a painting.

17
00:02:01,896 --> 00:02:02,896
With a splash.

18
00:02:49,521 --> 00:02:53,313
CLOSE TO ME

19
00:03:16,313 --> 00:03:17,313
Hi.

20
00:03:21,521 --> 00:03:22,896
All good?

21
00:03:23,021 --> 00:03:24,020
For you maybe!

22
00:03:24,021 --> 00:03:25,938
Five minutes in the sample room.

23
00:03:26,396 --> 00:03:28,521
For her, a month of hormones and surgery.

24
00:03:30,521 --> 00:03:32,063
Excuse me, doctor.

25
00:03:32,521 --> 00:03:33,813
You're right, Robi.

26
00:03:34,021 --> 00:03:35,521
We've been taking our time.

27
00:03:36,021 --> 00:03:37,896
We need the bed.
Get out of here.

28
00:03:38,021 --> 00:03:39,938
No, just a little longer, please?

29
00:03:40,813 --> 00:03:43,563
That anesthetic is a treat, I know.

30
00:03:44,521 --> 00:03:46,521
Some days... right, Robi?

31
00:03:48,146 --> 00:03:49,938
You don't want to know.

32
00:03:50,521 --> 00:03:55,896
Hey, remind me what we have to do now,
my brain is all foggy...

33
00:03:56,396 --> 00:03:58,937
You, nothing...
We'll take care of it.

34
00:03:58,938 --> 00:04:00,521
We'll fertilize all your eggs.

35
00:04:01,146 --> 00:04:03,938
Instead of Mr. Urinary Infection here.

36
00:04:06,896 --> 00:04:08,146
Come on, sweetie.

37
00:04:09,188 --> 00:04:10,813
My name is Luca Messico,

38
00:04:11,396 --> 00:04:13,270
son of Giovanni Messico,

39
00:04:13,271 --> 00:04:16,146
who retired but then died
while saving two kids from a fire.

40
00:04:17,396 --> 00:04:22,396
I always envied his courage.
He saw a house on fire and jumped in.

41
00:04:23,271 --> 00:04:27,313
I don't jump
I procrastinate.

42
00:04:28,771 --> 00:04:31,396
A man destined to have
a brilliant academic career,

43
00:04:31,521 --> 00:04:33,813
if only he finished his PhD thesis.

44
00:04:35,396 --> 00:04:37,896
A textbook case of self-sabotage.

45
00:04:39,146 --> 00:04:41,770
But this isn't the story
of how I finally finished

46
00:04:41,771 --> 00:04:45,438
my PhD thesis on Peter Sloterdijk
and the taming of mankind.

47
00:04:46,021 --> 00:04:51,020
As John Lennon said, "life is what
happens to you

48
00:04:51,021 --> 00:04:53,813
while you're busy making other plans."

49
00:04:54,438 --> 00:04:56,021
Honey, are you coming?

50
00:04:56,896 --> 00:04:57,896
Yes.

51
00:05:02,771 --> 00:05:04,521
Oh god, more images from Milan?

52
00:05:05,021 --> 00:05:07,521
Great timing for planning to have a baby.

53
00:05:08,521 --> 00:05:11,521
What are we going to do,
stay at home 24/7?

54
00:05:11,771 --> 00:05:14,270
Speak for yourself.
I spoke with the chief medical officer,

55
00:05:14,271 --> 00:05:16,438
I won't be at home much at all.

56
00:05:18,563 --> 00:05:22,063
What the hell am I going to do,
alone in here all the time?

57
00:05:23,021 --> 00:05:24,021
Write your thesis.

58
00:05:24,438 --> 00:05:27,771
You always say you want to finish it.
You've got all the time in the world.

59
00:05:29,813 --> 00:05:30,813
Use it.

60
00:05:31,771 --> 00:05:35,146
All Italians, from March 10, 2020,

61
00:05:35,271 --> 00:05:37,271
had their lives turned upside down.

62
00:05:37,896 --> 00:05:41,063
But this isn't the story
of how the Covid-19 pandemic

63
00:05:41,188 --> 00:05:43,396
derailed our entire existence.

64
00:05:46,896 --> 00:05:49,021
I thought we had to limit our contacts...

65
00:05:49,146 --> 00:05:51,813
Come on, it might be
our last dinner, for a while.

66
00:05:52,021 --> 00:05:54,021
And it has to be with him?

67
00:05:54,521 --> 00:05:56,020
He didn't charge us.

68
00:05:56,021 --> 00:05:57,896
You can tolerate a little sarcasm.

69
00:05:58,021 --> 00:05:59,812
Why is it always about money for you?

70
00:05:59,813 --> 00:06:02,021
Why is it never about money for you?

71
00:06:08,021 --> 00:06:10,021
Hi, welcome.

72
00:06:11,438 --> 00:06:13,396
- Right on time. Unbelievable!
- Hi kiddo.

73
00:06:13,521 --> 00:06:14,896
Better late than never.

74
00:06:15,271 --> 00:06:17,020
Speaking of better late than never.

75
00:06:17,021 --> 00:06:19,063
- Valerio...
- May I?

76
00:06:20,021 --> 00:06:22,521
- Hi, you.
- Do you remember your sister?

77
00:06:23,271 --> 00:06:24,896
- Hi Daria.
- Hi Sara.

78
00:06:25,271 --> 00:06:27,520
While we can still see
each other in person.

79
00:06:27,521 --> 00:06:28,813
Let's try, come in.

80
00:06:30,521 --> 00:06:33,146
Five minutes in the freezer,
just to be safe.

81
00:06:33,271 --> 00:06:35,896
- Yes, sir.
- FFP2 masks.

82
00:06:36,396 --> 00:06:39,146
Use them sparingly, they're
harder to find than white truffles.

83
00:06:39,271 --> 00:06:40,271
Ok.

84
00:06:40,438 --> 00:06:41,438
- Hi.
- Hi Luca.

85
00:06:42,563 --> 00:06:44,771
He's so cute! Sleepyhead.

86
00:06:44,896 --> 00:06:45,813
Thanks.

87
00:06:46,438 --> 00:06:48,520
- Wow, what a beautiful home.
- Thanks.

88
00:06:48,521 --> 00:06:50,813
You bet it is. I bought it for them.

89
00:06:51,021 --> 00:06:52,021
Antonello!

90
00:06:52,896 --> 00:06:55,021
Where exactly, along the Appia Antica?

91
00:06:55,438 --> 00:06:59,563
Just after the Cecilia Metella
Mausoleum, on the right.

92
00:07:00,896 --> 00:07:02,146
It's huge!

93
00:07:02,438 --> 00:07:03,771
How much did it cost?

94
00:07:03,938 --> 00:07:06,146
The mausoleum would have cost less.

95
00:07:07,396 --> 00:07:10,396
I'm getting old,
let me do whatever the hell I want.

96
00:07:10,521 --> 00:07:12,937
Honey, you're not dying.
Please!

97
00:07:12,938 --> 00:07:15,896
What's this hole, the swimming pool?

98
00:07:17,021 --> 00:07:20,521
20 x 6, infinity pool, salt water.

99
00:07:21,771 --> 00:07:25,938
But the idiots made it too deep.
What am I, an Olympic diver?

100
00:07:26,396 --> 00:07:30,020
I'm making them fill it up with dirt,
so I can pour another load of concrete.

101
00:07:30,021 --> 00:07:32,021
Unless they shut the construction down.

102
00:07:32,146 --> 00:07:34,521
This Covid is a pain in the ass!

103
00:07:34,896 --> 00:07:38,021
I'll have a half-finished villa
for who knows how long.

104
00:07:38,521 --> 00:07:41,146
It doesn't seem like the most
serious problem in the world right now,

105
00:07:41,271 --> 00:07:42,521
with all due respect.

106
00:07:45,021 --> 00:07:47,896
I get it, you're offended
by what I said earlier,

107
00:07:48,021 --> 00:07:50,271
but this house is clearly not something

108
00:07:50,396 --> 00:07:53,396
an ER doctor and a teacher
could afford, right?

109
00:07:53,521 --> 00:07:56,021
Daria could figure it out on her own.

110
00:07:57,188 --> 00:07:58,020
Come on...

111
00:07:58,021 --> 00:07:59,395
I know where this is going...

112
00:07:59,396 --> 00:08:01,771
He's going to bring up the Clinic again.

113
00:08:02,021 --> 00:08:05,396
When you graduated from medical school,
I was the happiest man in the world.

114
00:08:05,521 --> 00:08:07,896
What can I say?
I feel more useful in the hospital.

115
00:08:08,021 --> 00:08:09,520
- Ah, "useful".
- Yes, useful!

116
00:08:09,521 --> 00:08:12,895
But when you needed help
you came to the Clinic, didn't you?

117
00:08:12,896 --> 00:08:14,895
Do you even hear yourself?

118
00:08:14,896 --> 00:08:17,521
If you wanted to turn down a lucrative job,

119
00:08:17,771 --> 00:08:21,896
you should've married a man
with a certain position.

120
00:08:22,021 --> 00:08:23,271
With all due respect.

121
00:08:23,521 --> 00:08:26,812
You might have a tumor
pressing against your frontal lobe.

122
00:08:26,813 --> 00:08:29,521
It would explain
your total lack of inhibition.

123
00:08:30,021 --> 00:08:34,188
See how he learns, our professor.
That's a medical joke.

124
00:08:34,313 --> 00:08:36,021
And a good one. Well done!

125
00:08:36,188 --> 00:08:39,021
I like the fact that my husband
is not ambitious.

126
00:08:41,521 --> 00:08:42,438
Who is it, now?

127
00:08:42,563 --> 00:08:44,021
I dunno, I'll go see.

128
00:08:44,271 --> 00:08:47,021
The Grim Reaper,
like in that Monty Python movie.

129
00:08:47,438 --> 00:08:49,896
Would you cut it out
with these jokes about death?

130
00:08:50,021 --> 00:08:52,812
Sorry, you should touch wood.
That's chipboard. I bought it.

131
00:08:52,813 --> 00:08:53,896
Oh, sorry...

132
00:08:58,521 --> 00:09:02,813
This is the story of Amanda,
and how she ruined my life.

133
00:09:03,438 --> 00:09:04,438
Yes?

134
00:09:05,146 --> 00:09:06,771
I'm staying at the B&B down the hall.

135
00:09:06,896 --> 00:09:09,521
To get in you need a code,
but my battery is dead,

136
00:09:09,813 --> 00:09:11,396
and the code is on my phone.

137
00:09:11,563 --> 00:09:14,396
Too much information.
What do you need?

138
00:09:14,563 --> 00:09:16,396
Can I charge my phone for a minute?

139
00:09:16,521 --> 00:09:17,896
Yeah, sure, of course.

140
00:09:18,938 --> 00:09:22,020
The plug is right there.
It should work...

141
00:09:22,021 --> 00:09:24,021
- Who is it?
- The neighbor, honey!

142
00:09:24,813 --> 00:09:25,813
What neighbor?

143
00:09:27,396 --> 00:09:29,437
A girl staying in the B&B next door.

144
00:09:29,438 --> 00:09:32,896
She needs to charge her phone
to get into the apartment.

145
00:09:33,313 --> 00:09:34,438
Sorry to bother you.

146
00:09:34,771 --> 00:09:35,771
It's no trouble.

147
00:09:37,771 --> 00:09:39,437
So someone actually lives in this building!

148
00:09:39,438 --> 00:09:43,271
No neighbors,
no problems, remember that.

149
00:09:43,438 --> 00:09:45,896
A building full of offices is a real luxury.

150
00:09:46,021 --> 00:09:47,521
The Prime Minister is making an announcement.

151
00:09:47,896 --> 00:09:48,896
There he is.

152
00:09:49,021 --> 00:09:51,146
That is why I'm about to sign a decree

153
00:09:51,896 --> 00:09:54,771
that we can sum up with the expression:

154
00:09:55,021 --> 00:09:56,521
"I'm staying at home".

155
00:09:57,271 --> 00:10:00,021
There will no longer be a red zone.

156
00:10:00,313 --> 00:10:05,438
There will no longer be a zone
one and a zone two in our country.

157
00:10:06,021 --> 00:10:11,021
There will be one Italy,
one protected zone.

158
00:10:11,521 --> 00:10:17,521
Traveling is therefore restricted
throughout the nation,

159
00:10:18,021 --> 00:10:20,396
unless it is motivated

160
00:10:20,896 --> 00:10:23,146
by one of three specific circumstances:

161
00:10:23,813 --> 00:10:26,396
business reasons,

162
00:10:28,271 --> 00:10:33,146
cases of necessity or health reasons.

163
00:10:34,313 --> 00:10:41,146
We are also banning outdoor gatherings.

164
00:10:41,521 --> 00:10:42,521
Right...

165
00:10:44,521 --> 00:10:46,021
We'd better get going.

166
00:10:46,146 --> 00:10:48,020
If he wakes up,
we're doomed, Sara.

167
00:10:48,021 --> 00:10:49,271
God help us.

168
00:10:50,021 --> 00:10:53,396
I thought I was done with all this forever...

169
00:10:53,521 --> 00:10:55,437
Fertility is your speciality.

170
00:10:55,438 --> 00:10:56,896
Unbelievable.

171
00:10:57,021 --> 00:10:58,896
I can, and he can't.

172
00:10:59,313 --> 00:11:01,313
He's not the problem. Stop it.

173
00:11:01,521 --> 00:11:02,521
He isn't?

174
00:11:03,188 --> 00:11:05,895
Don't you know that the water in Rome
is full of estrogen?

175
00:11:05,896 --> 00:11:08,771
A concentrate of female hormones.
Sooner or later...

176
00:11:10,521 --> 00:11:12,396
I'll help you clear the table.

177
00:11:12,521 --> 00:11:13,438
No, no.

178
00:11:16,146 --> 00:11:19,396
How long have you been staying
in the B&B? I thought it was empty.

179
00:11:19,771 --> 00:11:20,771
A few days.

180
00:11:24,021 --> 00:11:25,271
You might be stuck for a while.

181
00:11:25,396 --> 00:11:27,021
Did you hear?
Lockdown starts tomorrow.

182
00:11:27,146 --> 00:11:28,146
Yeah.

183
00:11:28,938 --> 00:11:31,146
What the hell am I supposed to do,
barricaded inside?

184
00:11:31,521 --> 00:11:33,271
If I can ever get in.

185
00:11:34,146 --> 00:11:36,188
Luca, by the way. Nice to meet you.

186
00:11:36,521 --> 00:11:37,521
Amanda.

187
00:11:39,146 --> 00:11:41,896
Like the protagonist of
'Bright Lights, Big City'.

188
00:11:49,271 --> 00:11:50,896
Why is it taking so long?

189
00:11:52,396 --> 00:11:53,396
Are you leaving?

190
00:11:53,521 --> 00:11:56,438
Going home,
for good it seems.

191
00:11:57,021 --> 00:11:58,313
- Hang in there.
- Sure.

192
00:11:58,896 --> 00:12:01,896
- 'Night Luca, thanks for everything.
- Bye. Don't mention it.

193
00:12:04,521 --> 00:12:06,813
- Goodbye.
- Goodbye.

194
00:12:09,396 --> 00:12:10,396
Have we met?

195
00:12:11,521 --> 00:12:12,438
No.

196
00:12:12,563 --> 00:12:14,313
Dad, please. "Have we met?".

197
00:12:14,813 --> 00:12:15,813
Goodbye.

198
00:12:15,938 --> 00:12:17,271
- What did I say?
- Go.

199
00:12:17,521 --> 00:12:18,813
- Bye.
- Bye, Sara.

200
00:12:20,771 --> 00:12:22,396
Bye, you! Fast asleep.

201
00:12:22,521 --> 00:12:25,521
- Show some affection!
- You're talking of affection?

202
00:12:25,896 --> 00:12:26,896
Go on.

203
00:12:27,521 --> 00:12:28,521
- Bye.
- Bye.

204
00:12:29,021 --> 00:12:30,188
Bye, good night.

205
00:12:34,146 --> 00:12:36,438
- My name's Sara.
- Hi Sara.

206
00:12:37,896 --> 00:12:39,021
- And you are?
- Amanda.

207
00:12:39,271 --> 00:12:40,270
Amanda.

208
00:12:40,271 --> 00:12:42,812
Sorry for intruding,
I didn't know what else to do.

209
00:12:42,813 --> 00:12:43,896
Don't mention it.

210
00:12:44,021 --> 00:12:45,396
I'll go clear the table.

211
00:12:49,021 --> 00:12:50,521
- It came back on!
- Thank God.

212
00:12:52,521 --> 00:12:55,271
There it is, 014217.

213
00:12:58,396 --> 00:12:59,396
Got it?

214
00:13:00,063 --> 00:13:01,021
I think so.

215
00:13:02,396 --> 00:13:03,521
- Thanks.
- No problem.

216
00:13:07,938 --> 00:13:08,896
Zero fourteen...

217
00:13:10,021 --> 00:13:12,271
- Zero fourteen twenty-one seven.
- Right.

218
00:13:16,021 --> 00:13:18,146
Ok. Thanks again.

219
00:13:18,313 --> 00:13:19,313
Bye. Good night.

220
00:13:28,938 --> 00:13:31,438
No, I wouldn't say
she was rude, poor thing.

221
00:13:32,021 --> 00:13:33,146
She was embarrassed.

222
00:13:34,146 --> 00:13:36,438
I would be too, if I married an old man.

223
00:13:39,396 --> 00:13:41,896
I'm not going to be friends with her, mom.

224
00:13:42,271 --> 00:13:44,896
The problem here is dad, not Daria.

225
00:13:46,146 --> 00:13:48,521
Alright, I have to go now, ok?

226
00:13:51,063 --> 00:13:52,521
Yes, I'll be careful. Bye.

227
00:13:54,021 --> 00:13:56,896
Obviously, it's a gorgeous day,
now that we can't go out.

228
00:13:57,021 --> 00:13:58,271
I mean, I can't.

229
00:13:58,771 --> 00:14:01,021
Going to the hospital
isn't exactly going out.

230
00:14:01,313 --> 00:14:03,021
Any coffee left?

231
00:14:03,313 --> 00:14:05,896
Of course. Who do you take me for?

232
00:14:10,521 --> 00:14:12,521
I was thinking...

233
00:14:13,563 --> 00:14:15,896
Should we reschedule it?

234
00:14:17,521 --> 00:14:19,521
The IVF, you mean?

235
00:14:21,396 --> 00:14:23,188
I don't know, honey, it's up to you.

236
00:14:23,396 --> 00:14:26,020
Come on, don't leave me
all the responsibility.

237
00:14:26,021 --> 00:14:27,521
Tell me, what do you think?

238
00:14:27,771 --> 00:14:29,021
- I just woke up.
- Right.

239
00:14:29,938 --> 00:14:31,271
Hey, calm down.

240
00:14:33,021 --> 00:14:36,521
Whenever we talk about the baby,
you make me feel alone.

241
00:14:37,521 --> 00:14:38,896
You're not alone.

242
00:14:40,438 --> 00:14:41,771
What should we do?

243
00:14:43,271 --> 00:14:45,021
There's a fucking pandemic,

244
00:14:45,313 --> 00:14:48,021
it doesn't seem wise
to have an operation now.

245
00:14:50,021 --> 00:14:51,271
Let's reschedule it.

246
00:14:53,438 --> 00:14:54,438
You're right.

247
00:14:54,896 --> 00:14:55,896
Ok.

248
00:14:57,146 --> 00:14:58,146
Fine.

249
00:15:02,438 --> 00:15:03,521
How do I look?

250
00:15:04,021 --> 00:15:05,396
Miss Afghanistan.

251
00:15:06,438 --> 00:15:07,521
What are you up to?

252
00:15:08,021 --> 00:15:10,021
I have a zoom call with
the other teachers,

253
00:15:10,146 --> 00:15:11,146
then nothing.

254
00:15:11,271 --> 00:15:12,771
Well, write your thesis.

255
00:15:14,063 --> 00:15:16,396
- When are you coming back?
- Wish I knew!

256
00:15:17,771 --> 00:15:18,771
Bye.

257
00:15:18,938 --> 00:15:20,146
- Bye.
- Have a nice day.

258
00:15:21,021 --> 00:15:22,021
You too.

259
00:15:25,021 --> 00:15:26,438
I am ambitious, by the way.

260
00:15:27,313 --> 00:15:29,396
I knew you'd be upset about it.

261
