01:18:11,563 --> 01:18:13,188
Put that thing down.
Put that thing down!

1041
01:18:13,521 --> 01:18:14,521
- Drop it!
- Yes, ok.

1042
01:18:14,813 --> 01:18:16,770
- Who the fuck are you?
- Leave him alone.

1043
01:18:16,771 --> 01:18:17,813
Shut up!

1044
01:18:18,188 --> 01:18:19,646
How did you get in here?

1045
01:18:19,771 --> 01:18:22,520
How does this asshole know the code?
Are you screwing him?

1046
01:18:22,521 --> 01:18:24,270
I'm just the neighbor,
I heard someone shouting.

1047
01:18:24,271 --> 01:18:26,771
Ah, the neighbor?
Did you make that video?

1048
01:18:27,021 --> 01:18:29,813
- No... What video?
- Bullshit. Don't you bullshit me!

1049
01:18:30,021 --> 01:18:32,521
I know who you are.
You're Sara Bernini's husband.

1050
01:18:32,646 --> 01:18:34,521
- Cosimo no, please.
- You shut up!

1051
01:18:36,188 --> 01:18:38,688
So now you're fucking
your sister's husband?

1052
01:18:39,563 --> 01:18:41,188
- What?!
- What?!

1053
01:18:41,521 --> 01:18:44,688
You seriously didn't know?
Really? Wanna know why?

1054
01:18:44,813 --> 01:18:48,021
Because she, in addition
to being a whore, is also mentally-

1055
01:18:56,771 --> 01:18:57,771
You killed him.

1056
01:19:17,521 --> 01:19:21,813
When it was all over,
I had a sudden revelation:

1057
01:19:22,646 --> 01:19:24,438
not only was I not the hero,

1058
01:19:24,771 --> 01:19:27,021
I wasn't even
the main character in this story.

1059
01:19:27,688 --> 01:19:30,146
You suffer from polycystic ovary disease.

1060
01:19:30,271 --> 01:19:32,521
Have you ever been diagnosed with it?

1061
01:19:33,813 --> 01:19:34,813
No.

1062
01:19:38,188 --> 01:19:39,896
Why did you choose to come to our clinic?

1063
01:19:41,021 --> 01:19:42,188
I wanted to meet you.

1064
01:19:44,063 --> 01:19:46,146
Because of that interview
I did on TV, right?

1065
01:19:47,438 --> 01:19:51,188
You can't guess how many women
came here afterwards.

1066
01:19:52,563 --> 01:19:53,521
Goodbye, Doctor.

1067
01:20:01,438 --> 01:20:05,771
You didn't tell me if you wanted to go
through with artificial insemination.

1068
01:20:06,063 --> 01:20:08,646
I wanted to understand
a few things first.

1069
01:20:09,813 --> 01:20:10,813
About myself.

1070
01:20:12,146 --> 01:20:14,521
Your condition is nothing to worry about.

1071
01:20:14,646 --> 01:20:17,688
It's fairly frequent.
My daughter has the same problem.

1072
01:20:18,521 --> 01:20:19,521
Your daughter?

1073
01:20:20,271 --> 01:20:22,146
My one unrequited love.

1074
01:20:23,271 --> 01:20:24,271
How old is she?

1075
01:20:25,271 --> 01:20:26,771
About your age, I'd guess.

1076
01:20:28,313 --> 01:20:29,313
What's her name?

1077
01:20:29,521 --> 01:20:30,521
Sara.

1078
01:20:32,146 --> 01:20:33,145
Why?

1079
01:20:33,146 --> 01:20:34,188
Goodbye.

1080
01:20:34,688 --> 01:20:35,688
Goodbye.

1081
01:20:36,938 --> 01:20:40,521
All that time I thought I was the one
spying on Amanda, from my window.

1082
01:20:41,771 --> 01:20:44,146
But actually, it was she who spied on us.

1083
01:20:46,313 --> 01:20:48,271
It's a bit like the fish
in that Australian aquarium.

1084
01:20:48,771 --> 01:20:52,021
The tourists thought
the fish were the show.

1085
01:20:52,271 --> 01:20:56,646
But from the fish's point of view,
the humans were the show.

1086
01:20:57,813 --> 01:20:59,938
With no more visitors,
they got depressed.

1087
01:21:03,146 --> 01:21:06,688
In the end, life is just
a point of view.

1088
01:21:32,813 --> 01:21:34,771
He helped me find Sara's address.

1089
01:21:37,688 --> 01:21:40,271
But then he realized
I had come to stay here.

1090
01:21:42,771 --> 01:21:45,146
You've been lying to me the whole time.

1091
01:21:45,521 --> 01:21:48,188
What happened between us
wasn't part of my plan.

1092
01:21:50,063 --> 01:21:52,646
I just wanted to have
a peek at Sara's life,

1093
01:21:53,646 --> 01:21:56,771
to understand why she had everything
and I had nothing.

1094
01:21:59,146 --> 01:22:00,688
But then the lockdown came.

1095
01:22:02,313 --> 01:22:03,688
I was locked up in here,

1096
01:22:07,146 --> 01:22:08,771
and you started looking at me.

1097
01:22:09,938 --> 01:22:11,187
Oh, so now it's my fault?

1098
01:22:11,188 --> 01:22:13,521
How the fuck was I supposed to know
you were my wife's sister?

1099
01:22:14,063 --> 01:22:16,646
I never planned
on falling in love with you.

1100
01:22:24,271 --> 01:22:25,271
What a mess.

1101
01:22:26,188 --> 01:22:28,646
He was about to shoot you,
what was I supposed to do?

1102
01:22:29,021 --> 01:22:31,063
Sorry if I saved your life.

1103
01:22:31,438 --> 01:22:32,688
Thank you very much.

1104
01:22:35,563 --> 01:22:39,021
Now they're going to send me to jail
and throw away the key.

1105
01:22:40,146 --> 01:22:43,271
- What could I have done?
- You could have left me out of this.

1106
01:22:43,438 --> 01:22:45,188
Did I force you to do anything?

1107
01:22:45,771 --> 01:22:47,188
We both wanted it.

1108
01:22:54,021 --> 01:22:55,438
No one saw him come here.

1109
01:22:57,188 --> 01:22:59,521
He couldn't exactly tell the other cops
he would come here.

1110
01:23:02,646 --> 01:23:05,438
There are only offices here,
and they're closed.

1111
01:23:06,438 --> 01:23:07,646
No one heard us.

1112
01:23:10,021 --> 01:23:11,021
So what?

1113
01:23:12,021 --> 01:23:12,938
Amanda.

1114
01:23:14,771 --> 01:23:16,271
Is that really your name?

1115
01:23:16,771 --> 01:23:17,771
Idiot.

1116
01:23:20,188 --> 01:23:21,188
Let's make a deal.

1117
01:23:23,521 --> 01:23:24,938
I'll take care of Cosimo,

1118
01:23:26,188 --> 01:23:29,146
but in return you leave
Sara and me alone, forever.

1119
01:23:33,813 --> 01:23:34,813
What do you say?

1120
01:23:36,813 --> 01:23:38,771
How are you going
to get rid of the body?

1121
01:23:42,021 --> 01:23:44,188
Antonello's villa on the Appia Antica.

1122
01:23:47,063 --> 01:23:50,813
The construction was suspended,
but it'll start up again tomorrow.

1123
01:23:51,771 --> 01:23:53,063
Got any garbage bags?

1124
01:24:08,188 --> 01:24:09,438
Who knows about the two of you?

1125
01:24:09,896 --> 01:24:10,896
No one.

1126
01:24:14,521 --> 01:24:15,521
I'm off.

1127
01:25:56,271 --> 01:25:59,021
Someone whose name escapes me
said that life is a tragedy

1128
01:25:59,146 --> 01:26:00,521
when seen in close-up,

1129
01:26:06,063 --> 01:26:09,188
but a comedy when seen
in a wide shot.

1130
01:26:18,021 --> 01:26:19,771
You may talk with my colleague.

1131
01:26:31,313 --> 01:26:36,771
The truth is, all irrational actions
are guided by rationality, basically.

1132
01:26:37,771 --> 01:26:43,896
There is always a logical reason for things
you cannot explain, in hindsight.

1133
01:27:01,438 --> 01:27:02,646
My own Xanadu.

1134
01:27:04,313 --> 01:27:05,688
But it's not finished!

1135
01:27:05,938 --> 01:27:08,188
Because of Covid, the work had to stop!

1136
01:27:08,438 --> 01:27:10,188
But everything we need is here.

1137
01:27:15,688 --> 01:27:19,521
Come on Robi, let's celebrate
the end of this damn quarantine!

1138
01:27:21,146 --> 01:27:25,271
...and he came in with that Buddha.

1139
01:27:31,646 --> 01:27:34,813
I can't remember anything else,
it all happened so fast.

1140
01:28:49,521 --> 01:28:50,521
Well, Doctor?

1141
01:28:50,688 --> 01:28:52,938
What are you up to?
Aren't you coming?

1142
01:28:53,271 --> 01:28:54,521
What's on your mind?

1143
01:28:56,771 --> 01:28:59,688
The end of the world,
that's what was on my mind,

1144
01:29:00,646 --> 01:29:01,688
can you believe it?

1145
01:29:05,063 --> 01:29:07,771
But you're way better
than the end of the world.

1146
01:29:08,021 --> 01:29:09,771
Look at you. You are fantastic.

1147
01:29:19,021 --> 01:29:20,021
Call from "Uppercase A".

1148
01:29:22,146 --> 01:29:23,146
What?

1149
01:29:23,688 --> 01:29:25,188
I want to change our deal.

1150
01:29:26,563 --> 01:29:29,188
What the fuck?
I just finished my part.

1151
01:29:29,646 --> 01:29:30,688
I am not my mother.

1152
01:29:31,146 --> 01:29:32,521
I'm not going anywhere.

1153
01:29:32,646 --> 01:29:34,771
- Are you trying to screw me over?
- No.

1154
01:29:35,188 --> 01:29:36,813
I'm turning you into a hero.

1155
01:29:38,021 --> 01:29:39,271
You were at your window

1156
01:29:39,813 --> 01:29:42,770
and you saw a man with
a gun attacking your neighbor.

1157
01:29:42,771 --> 01:29:43,813
Do you want this?

1158
01:29:45,021 --> 01:29:47,771
You ran to help her,
because you are a brave man.

1159
01:29:51,646 --> 01:29:52,771
The door was open.

1160
01:29:53,271 --> 01:29:57,271
You came up behind him and hit him
with the first thing you found:

1161
01:29:58,313 --> 01:30:01,688
the Buddha figurine,
which in fact has your fingerprints on it.

1162
01:30:03,063 --> 01:30:04,688
What the fuck are you saying?

1163
01:30:04,813 --> 01:30:07,271
You acted out of instinct,
or self-defense.

1164
01:30:07,688 --> 01:30:09,687
You saved my life and then,
since you were scared,

1165
01:30:09,688 --> 01:30:11,938
because he was a cop
and he was blackmailing me...

1166
01:30:12,146 --> 01:30:13,145
Cosimo Bravetta.

1167
01:30:13,146 --> 01:30:15,688
...you said you would get rid of the corpse.

1168
01:30:17,146 --> 01:30:18,146
You did it for me.

1169
01:30:22,563 --> 01:30:23,521
Who are you with?

1170
01:30:23,771 --> 01:30:25,687
Who are you telling this story to?

1171
01:30:25,688 --> 01:30:28,188
You're the one
who has to tell the story, Luca.

1172
01:30:28,521 --> 01:30:31,021
I told the police where
you buried the body.

1173
01:30:32,271 --> 01:30:33,271
You did what?

1174
01:30:34,521 --> 01:30:36,688
Your brilliant plan was terrible,
let's face it.

1175
01:30:36,938 --> 01:30:38,521
How long do you think
it would have taken them

1176
01:30:38,688 --> 01:30:40,271
to trace Cosimo's last movements
and learn about me?

1177
01:30:40,771 --> 01:30:41,771
You're crazy.

1178
01:30:42,146 --> 01:30:43,688
He was right, you are crazy!

1179
01:30:44,271 --> 01:30:46,521
You can become the hero you wanted to be.

1180
01:30:46,771 --> 01:30:50,271
Or else, you can tell the truth:
you were a coward,

1181
01:30:51,021 --> 01:30:54,313
you dropped the figurine,
you let me do the hard part,

1182
01:30:55,521 --> 01:30:57,145
and then offered to hide the body

1183
01:30:57,146 --> 01:30:59,271
on the condition
that I disappear from your life.

1184
01:31:00,021 --> 01:31:02,688
You're going to jail anyway,
as an accomplice.

1185
01:31:03,188 --> 01:31:05,813
But in that case,
I will also tell the truth.

1186
01:31:06,146 --> 01:31:07,688
To your wife, first of all.

1187
01:31:08,563 --> 01:31:10,688
If you're so innocent, like you say,

1188
01:31:11,188 --> 01:31:13,145
why didn't you tell me
she was your sister?

1189
01:31:13,146 --> 01:31:14,188
Why?!

1190
01:31:14,688 --> 01:31:15,688
I'll tell you why:

1191
01:31:17,563 --> 01:31:20,021
you planned it all, that's why.

1192
01:31:21,188 --> 01:31:22,938
You just wanted to hurt her.

1193
01:31:23,521 --> 01:31:26,521
If I wanted to hurt Sara,
I would have told her everything, right?

1194
01:31:28,438 --> 01:31:30,438
But no, she'll never know a thing.

1195
01:31:30,646 --> 01:31:32,521
Who are you? You're a monster.

1196
01:31:32,646 --> 01:31:34,063
Jesus, you're a monster.

1197
01:31:35,146 --> 01:31:36,146
Make up your mind, Luca:

1198
01:31:40,938 --> 01:31:41,938
the truth...

1199
01:31:42,146 --> 01:31:43,188
Turn off the engine!

1200
01:31:44,521 --> 01:31:47,271
... or the happiest possible ending
for all of us?

1201
01:31:48,813 --> 01:31:52,271
Good, now put your hands
where I can see them, on the wheel.

1202
01:31:57,563 --> 01:32:01,771
This isn't the story of how I got
myself arrested for murder.

1203
01:32:32,688 --> 01:32:36,646
No, officer, this is my house,
and that is my husband!

1204
01:32:44,813 --> 01:32:47,021
The investigators couldn't understand why

1205
01:32:47,146 --> 01:32:49,521
I hid the body
at my father-in-law's house.

1206
01:32:50,146 --> 01:32:52,688
But that's just because they
don't know my father-in-law.

1207
01:32:56,771 --> 01:32:58,646
This is my home,
I have to talk with my husband.

1208
01:32:58,896 --> 01:33:01,520
The construction site at his villa
was sealed off as a crime scene,

1209
01:33:01,521 --> 01:33:03,271
for who knows how long.

1210
01:33:25,146 --> 01:33:30,771
It's a small consolation to know
that after all, it is Antonello's fault.

1211
01:33:35,021 --> 01:33:36,021
Asshole!

1212
01:33:36,271 --> 01:33:40,688
Now that the lockdown was over and everyone
else was finally starting to go out again,

1213
01:33:41,313 --> 01:33:44,063
I was going to be locked up again...

1214
01:33:44,521 --> 01:33:45,938
... but this time, in jail.

1215
01:33:46,188 --> 01:33:48,813
Anyway, I'm glad Betta is your lawyer.

1216
01:33:49,188 --> 01:33:51,646
You're in good hands,
good for you. She's a tiger.

1217
01:33:52,188 --> 01:33:54,771
Yeah, I have more respect for her
more than I do for you, you know that.

1218
01:33:55,563 --> 01:33:56,813
Can't say you're wrong.

1219
01:34:04,021 --> 01:34:06,521
Tell me the truth: what did you feel
when you killed that piece of shit?

1220
01:34:09,021 --> 01:34:10,188
A sense of necessity.

1221
01:34:11,688 --> 01:34:12,688
What a man.

1222
01:34:13,188 --> 01:34:15,021
You're giving me a hard-on, I swear.

1223
01:34:15,271 --> 01:34:16,271
Moron.

1224
01:34:17,313 --> 01:34:18,313
Hey!

1225
01:34:21,021 --> 01:34:22,438
Know what I was thinking?

1226
01:34:22,688 --> 01:34:24,646
Your son will also have
a hero for a father.

1227
01:34:24,813 --> 01:34:26,146
Except, you survived.

1228
01:34:26,271 --> 01:34:29,021
You are the evolution
of the species, get it?

1229
01:34:31,021 --> 01:34:32,145
Goodbye, my friend.

1230
01:34:32,146 --> 01:34:33,188
Bye.

1231
01:34:34,771 --> 01:34:37,688
Besides, I was a bit of a hero, for real.

1232
01:34:38,021 --> 01:34:41,146
After all, I lifted that Buddha first.

1233
01:34:41,771 --> 01:34:43,688
I wasn't making everything up.

1234
01:34:48,896 --> 01:34:53,021
And even if I was a liar,
compared to her I was an amateur.

1235
01:35:13,688 --> 01:35:15,563
What the hell is this all about?

1236
01:35:16,271 --> 01:35:19,063
What is this letter supposed to mean?
Is it all true?

1237
01:35:19,688 --> 01:35:21,646
First of all, thanks for coming.

1238
01:35:21,813 --> 01:35:25,187
Couldn't you have explained things to me
right away, instead of making such a mess?

1239
01:35:25,188 --> 01:35:26,771
I didn't have the courage.

1240
01:35:30,813 --> 01:35:32,438
So, you and I are...

1241
01:35:33,063 --> 01:35:34,063
Yes.

1242
01:35:44,146 --> 01:35:45,188
What a fucking mess.

1243
01:35:51,271 --> 01:35:55,021
Listen, there's a frozen embryo
waiting to see what my intentions are.

1244
01:35:55,188 --> 01:35:57,146
But first I need to know
if you slept with him.

1245
01:35:57,271 --> 01:36:00,188
Sara, please,
don't get any ideas into your head.

1246
01:36:02,438 --> 01:36:05,063
Luca just made a video of me
from the window.

1247
01:36:05,771 --> 01:36:08,521
Then he tried to convince me
to press charges,

1248
01:36:09,188 --> 01:36:11,188
but I didn't want anyone to know.

1249
01:36:12,146 --> 01:36:13,563
It was all my fault.

1250
01:36:15,563 --> 01:36:17,563
So, it was an act of courage?

1251
01:36:20,271 --> 01:36:22,021
That doesn't sound like him.

1252
01:36:23,188 --> 01:36:25,438
Look, if it wasn't for him,
I wouldn't be here.

1253
01:36:25,813 --> 01:36:27,688
Why didn't he tell me anything?

1254
01:36:28,021 --> 01:36:31,771
- Maybe he didn't want to get you involved.
- I don't know what the fuck to do.

1255
01:36:32,021 --> 01:36:33,271
Do you understand that?

1256
01:36:34,771 --> 01:36:36,188
Of course I understand.

1257
01:36:40,521 --> 01:36:42,188
I even went to get an abortion.

1258
01:36:47,563 --> 01:36:49,188
but then I spat out the pill.

1259
01:36:51,771 --> 01:36:52,771
You're pregnant?!

1260
01:36:54,521 --> 01:36:55,563
Who is the father?

1261
01:36:56,146 --> 01:36:58,688
Cosimo, the cop.

1262
01:37:09,646 --> 01:37:13,438
If I can do it, you can, too.

1263
01:37:18,271 --> 01:37:21,188
Maybe we can be one big family.

1264
01:37:27,021 --> 01:37:29,771
This is all too... strange for me, sorry.

1265
01:37:30,021 --> 01:37:31,188
- Sara, please... Sara!
- No, no.

1266
01:37:43,813 --> 01:37:46,396
SIX MONTHS LATER

1267
01:37:46,521 --> 01:37:48,187
In the name of the Italian people,

1268
01:37:48,188 --> 01:37:53,563
and with reference to articles
533 and 535 of the penal procedure

1269
01:37:53,688 --> 01:38:00,188
and articles 81 and 584 of the penal code,
this court finds Luca Messico,

1270
01:38:00,438 --> 01:38:03,521
guilty of the crime of murder
in the second degree,

1271
01:38:04,188 --> 01:38:08,771
while rejecting the charge of voluntary
manslaughter per the indictment.

1272
01:38:09,313 --> 01:38:10,771
- Shame on you!
- Clowns!

1273
01:38:11,021 --> 01:38:12,438
This sentence is ridiculous.
It's disgusting.

1274
01:38:12,646 --> 01:38:13,646
Silence!

1275
01:38:15,688 --> 01:38:19,563
As well as being guilty of the crime
of aggravated concealment of a corpse,

1276
01:38:19,688 --> 01:38:22,563
pursuant to article
61 number 2 of the penal code.

1277
01:38:22,688 --> 01:38:27,146
He is sentenced to four years
and six months of imprisonment,

1278
01:38:27,271 --> 01:38:30,645
in addition to the payment of court
and custodial costs...

1279
01:38:30,646 --> 01:38:32,188
Two years, and you're out.

1280
01:38:32,688 --> 01:38:34,062
Four and a half years...

1281
01:38:34,063 --> 01:38:36,145
That decided, this hearing is adjourned.

1282
01:38:36,146 --> 01:38:37,313
This is a travesty!

1283
01:38:38,688 --> 01:38:40,646
She says I'll be out in two years.

1284
01:38:45,688 --> 01:38:46,688
Dad, please!

1285
01:38:55,271 --> 01:38:59,896
This is not even the story
of how I became a father, twice.

1286
01:39:00,688 --> 01:39:02,063
With two different mothers.

1287
01:39:02,771 --> 01:39:03,771
Who are sisters.

1288
01:39:04,563 --> 01:39:06,188
Amanda! Wait.

1289
01:39:06,313 --> 01:39:10,688
Sweetie, can I talk to you for a minute?
Just a minute? Sara? Sara!

1290
01:39:11,146 --> 01:39:12,563
Sara, I'm your father!

1291
01:39:14,146 --> 01:39:17,646
This is the story of Amanda
and how she ruined my life.

1292
01:39:19,896 --> 01:39:22,313
I did a lot of bad things, for her.

1293
01:39:22,688 --> 01:39:24,521
Recreation! Everyone, outside!

1294
01:39:24,771 --> 01:39:28,146
I'm not at all the good citizen
the newspapers talk about.

1295
01:39:28,313 --> 01:39:30,271
I'm paying for a crime I didn't commit.

1296
01:39:31,521 --> 01:39:33,813
If you never take any responsibility,

1297
01:39:34,688 --> 01:39:37,188
life chooses one for you.

1298
01:39:44,688 --> 01:39:46,520
I have no idea how long it will take

1299
01:39:46,521 --> 01:39:48,271
for Amanda's mountain of lies
to come crashing down.

1300
01:39:48,646 --> 01:39:52,145
Nor what my child,
or rather my children,

1301
01:39:52,146 --> 01:39:53,896
will think of what happened,
years from now.

1302
01:39:56,271 --> 01:39:59,271
If nothing else, I've started
writing my PhD thesis.

1303
01:39:59,938 --> 01:40:02,271
I have all the time in the world
to finish it.

1304
01:40:02,938 --> 01:40:05,521
I'm not doing it to get back
into my university career.

1305
01:40:05,813 --> 01:40:07,188
It's too late for that.

1306
01:40:07,813 --> 01:40:09,271
I'm doing it for myself.

1307
01:40:09,688 --> 01:40:13,313
Come to think of it, this is
the story of how, for the first time,

1308
01:40:14,271 --> 01:40:17,188
I finished something I had started.

1309
01:40:21,146 --> 01:40:24,855
CLOSE TO ME

